      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"128 glyphs of 16 rows, glyph n at n * 16: row r of a character code's glyph is byte (code\nAND $7F) * 16 + r. The dots are bits 7-3, bit 7 leftmost; bits 2-0 are not drawn. Codes\n$80-$FF are block graphics, which the video makes itself, not from this ROM (Klive's core,\nht1080z-video.c).\nCode $00: a symbol; Series I/II never show it, as their video draws codes $00-$1F with the\nglyphs of $40-$5F."},
